ounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_19", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_20", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_17", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "No time-respecting cascade from 303 to 1293 exists in [28296,66695] under a 600-unit relay limit: 303 reaches only 10 nodes and neither of 1293's in-neighbours (28, 1438), and no candidate paths are enumerated. The negative is robust because relaxing the delay entirely still fails to reach 1293, showing the obstruction is event ordering rather than the wait budget. A static route 303->1583->28->1293 does exist, which is exactly the order-ignoring artifact to be discounted; likewise the intermediaries are hyperactive hubs (node 28: 600 events, 428 partners; steady 55-216 events per bin), so neither volume nor popularity can substitute for a valid temporal ordering. 303's own events all occur in the later half of the window while 1293's incoming contacts cluster earlier, so the prerequisite interactions precede the potential source signal. The reverse direction is also unreachable, ruling out a direction artifact."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Static connectivity exists but is temporally void:**\n- A static path 303 \u2192 1583 \u2192 28 \u2192 1293 exists (step_18, step_19, step_08), so an order-ignoring analysis would wrongly suggest a cascade.\n- Yet with the 600-unit relay constraint, 303 reaches only **10 nodes** and never 1293 (step_01); no paths are returned at all (step_15).\n- Critically, **even with no wait limit whatsoever**, 303 reaches 85 nodes and still fails to reach 1293 (step_04). The failure is one of event *ordering*, not of the delay budget.\n\n**Why the static route fails:** 303 cannot temporally reach either of 1293's two in-neighbours, 28 (step_10) or 1438 (step_11). The bridge is unusable in the required direction/order.\n\n**Timing explains the block:** 303's four events all fall in the *second half* of the window (\u226547496, step_12/step_14), whereas 1293's incoming contacts cluster earlier (bins at 28296\u201333095 and 42696\u201347495, step_13). The prerequisite interactions largely precede 303's activity.\n\n**Confounders ruled out:**\n- *Volume/popularity:* the intermediaries are hyperactive hubs \u2014 node 28 has 600 events and 428 distinct partners (step_09), and 28+1583 sustain 55\u2013216 events per bin across the whole window (step_20). Abundant hub traffic still yields no valid ordering.\n- *Reverse direction:* 1293 \u2192 303 is also unreachable (step_17), so this is not a mislabelled-direction artifact.\n- Both endpoints are low-degree (4 events each, step_03) within a dense 8,360-event graph (step_02) \u2014 activity volume belongs to the hubs, not the endpoints.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_44f03991\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [303, 1293],\n  \"window\": [28296, 66695],\n  \"confidence\": 0.91,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_18\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_19\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_20\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_17\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"No time-respecting cascade from 303 to 1293 exists in [28296,66695] under a 600-unit relay limit: 303 reaches only 10 nodes and neither of 1293's in-neighbours (28, 1438), and no candidate paths are enumerated. The negative is robust because relaxing the delay entirely still fails to reach 1293, showing the obstruction is event ordering rather than the wait budget. A static route 303->1583->28->1293 does exist, which is exactly the order-ignoring artifact to be discounted; likewise the intermediaries are hyperactive hubs (node 28: 600 events, 428 partners; steady 55-216 events per bin), so neither volume nor popularity can substitute for a valid temporal ordering. 303's own events all occur in the later half of the window while 1293's incoming contacts cluster earlier, so the prerequisite interactions precede the potential source signal. The reverse direction is also unreachable, ruling out a direction artifact.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 82978, "total_output_tokens": 5391, "total_tokens": 88369, "total_latency_ms": 79804, "llm_calls": 10, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}